        "title": "test(shared): add unit tests for safe-record defensive guards",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`isRecordWithoutThrowing`, `readRecordValue`, `copyArrayEntries`, and `copyRecordEntries` are exported defensive guards against hostile Proxy objects with 0% test coverage.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx -e \"\nimport { isRecordWithoutThrowing, readRecordValue, copyArrayEntries } from './src/shared/safe-record.js';\nconst hostile = new Proxy({}, { get() { throw new Error('boom'); } });\nconsole.log('throwing Proxy:', isRecordWithoutThrowing(hostile), '(typeof/Array.isArray are trap-safe)');\nconsole.log('readRecordValue on Proxy:', readRecordValue(hostile, 'key'), '(get trap caught → undefined)');\nconsole.log('readRecordValue normal:', readRecordValue({name:'test'}, 'name'));\nconsole.log('null copyArrayEntries:', JSON.stringify(copyArrayEntries(null)));\n\"\n\nthrowing Proxy: true (typeof/Array.isArray are trap-safe)\nreadRecordValue on Proxy: undefined (get trap caught → undefined)\nreadRecordValue normal: test\nnull copyArrayEntries: []\n\n$ npx vitest run src/shared/safe-record.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  15 passed (15)\n```\n",
